WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.428 --> 00:00:13.495
"Hello and to the Little Fox Animal Report.

2
00:00:14.296 --> 00:00:16.957
I am your host, Ian Shelback.

3
00:00:17.417 --> 00:00:20.219
Tonight, I am in Forest, Canada.

4
00:00:20.799 --> 00:00:25.422
I am interviewing a very special red fox named Boxer.

5
00:00:26.322 --> 00:00:29.004
He is the oldest fox in this forest.

6
00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:31.720
Good evening, Boxer."

7
00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:34.021
"Good evening, Ian."

8
00:00:34.041 --> 00:00:37.882
"Boxer, can you tell us about your life?

9
00:00:38.562 --> 00:00:41.403
What's life like here in the Canadian forest?"

10
00:00:41.423 --> 00:00:46.504
"Well, Ian, I would be delighted to tell you about my life.

11
00:00:48.585 --> 00:00:49.985
Where should I begin?

12
00:00:50.785 --> 00:00:54.947
Let me tell you about how I met my darling wife, Bridget.

13
00:00:58.127 --> 00:01:02.257
When I was a young fox, I left my family.

14
00:01:02.898 --> 00:01:05.099
I wanted to see the world.

15
00:01:05.119 --> 00:01:07.281
'Good luck, Boxer.

16
00:01:07.761 --> 00:01:08.502
Take care.'

17
00:01:08.522 --> 00:01:10.463
'Good-bye, Mother.

18
00:01:10.924 --> 00:01:12.145
Good-bye, Father.

19
00:01:12.565 --> 00:01:13.926
Good-bye, Family.'

20
00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:21.331
I traveled for almost one month.

21
00:01:22.012 --> 00:01:27.136
It was late summer so the forest was green and full of small animals.

22
00:01:27.888 --> 00:01:31.251
I especially liked to catch rabbits and birds.

23
00:01:32.252 --> 00:01:38.897
One day, while I was chasing a squirrel through a meadow, I met the prettiest vixen I have

24
00:01:39.217 --> 00:01:40.539
ever seen.

25
00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:49.906
Her face and ears were wonderfully pointed; her fur was long and her tail was very bushy.

26
00:01:50.827 --> 00:01:54.750
I don't think she weighed more than 3.6 kilograms.

27
00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:56.812
She was very slim.

28
00:01:58.344 --> 00:02:00.105
'Hello, I'm Bridget.

29
00:02:00.645 --> 00:02:02.465
I have never seen you before.'

30
00:02:02.485 --> 00:02:05.786
'Well hello, I'm Boxer.

31
00:02:06.627 --> 00:02:09.227
I am from very far away.

32
00:02:09.247 --> 00:02:13.329
I have been traveling through the forest.'

33
00:02:13.349 --> 00:02:17.510
'Traveling! That sounds exciting!

34
00:02:18.230 --> 00:02:20.071
I have lived here all my life.

35
00:02:20.791 --> 00:02:25.172
I would like to AHH!'

36
00:02:25.192 --> 00:02:32.318
Just then, a large wolf jumped out from behind a tree and tried to make us his supper.

37
00:02:33.059 --> 00:02:39.144
As quick as I could, I grabbed Bridget and we ran into a small hole.

38
00:02:39.744 --> 00:02:41.386
We barely escaped.

39
00:02:43.487 --> 00:02:49.332
From that day forward, we fell in love and lived happily together."

40
00:02:49.352 --> 00:02:51.954
"Did you build a house for your wife?"

41
00:02:51.974 --> 00:02:57.571
"Ian, red foxes don't like to have permanent houses.

42
00:02:58.212 --> 00:03:01.014
We usually spend our time outside.

43
00:03:01.755 --> 00:03:08.741
Even in the winter, when the other animals are hibernating, we play outside in the snow.

44
00:03:09.842 --> 00:03:14.627
By late December, it was time for us to start our family.

45
00:03:15.307 --> 00:03:20.052
I searched and searched for the best place to build a den.

46
00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:24.742
A den needs to be warm and dry for the cubs.

47
00:03:24.762 --> 00:03:28.663
'Boxer, we must find a den soon.

48
00:03:29.304 --> 00:03:31.465
Our cubs will come very soon.'

49
00:03:31.485 --> 00:03:33.665
'Don't worry, Bridget.

50
00:03:34.286 --> 00:03:37.087
I have found a great place for a den.

51
00:03:37.867 --> 00:03:40.388
It is an old groundhog's den.

52
00:03:40.408 --> 00:03:43.469
It is not too far away.'

53
00:03:44.510 --> 00:03:51.289
That very night, after we had settled into our new den, our cubs were born.

54
00:03:51.309 --> 00:03:58.474
We had six wonderful young cubs, three boys and three girls.

55
00:03:59.075 --> 00:04:00.656
It was terrific."

56
00:04:02.497 --> 00:04:05.559
"What was it like taking care of six young cubs?

57
00:04:06.260 --> 00:04:08.201
It must have been very hard work."

58
00:04:08.822 --> 00:04:11.063
"Well, it certainly was.

59
00:04:11.504 --> 00:04:17.368
You know, when they are born they cannot even see for nine days.

60
00:04:18.732 --> 00:04:22.976
Over the next two months the cubs grew and grew.

61
00:04:23.436 --> 00:04:26.839
Soon they were ready for their hunting lessons.

62
00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:29.481
'Okay, Children.

63
00:04:30.041 --> 00:04:33.624
Today you are going to get your first hunting lesson.

64
00:04:34.485 --> 00:04:40.670
Usually, we like to hunt these animals: rabbits, squirrels, and mice.

65
00:04:41.891 --> 00:04:44.973
Today, we will practice catching mice.

66
00:04:45.814 --> 00:04:51.357
Mice are not easy to catch so you will have to pay close attention.'

67
00:04:52.318 --> 00:04:58.040
After six months, Bridget and I had to say good-bye to our cubs.

68
00:04:58.680 --> 00:05:03.082
They were ready to go out into the world on their own.

69
00:05:03.102 --> 00:05:06.284
'Good-bye, my lovely cubs.

70
00:05:06.324 --> 00:05:06.964
Take care.

71
00:05:07.704 --> 00:05:09.005
Watch out for wolves!'

72
00:05:09.025 --> 00:05:13.087
'Good-bye, Mother; good-bye, Father.'

73
00:05:13.107 --> 00:05:15.888
'Good-bye, Children.'

74
00:05:17.940 --> 00:05:24.203
Bridget and I lived many happy years together and had many more wonderful cubs.

75
00:05:24.883 --> 00:05:27.424
My life has been great."

76
00:05:27.944 --> 00:05:30.985
"Well, thank you, Boxer.

77
00:05:31.446 --> 00:05:33.246
It has been great talking to you."

78
00:05:33.266 --> 00:05:41.610
"Before I go, I would like to say that I know that some people think foxes are mean

79
00:05:41.850 --> 00:05:44.811
and cunning, but we are not.

80
00:05:45.511 --> 00:05:48.925
We are kind and gentle."

81
00:05:48.945 --> 00:05:50.687
"Of course you are.

82
00:05:51.687 --> 00:05:53.549
That was Boxer the fox.

83
00:05:54.149 --> 00:06:00.874
This has been Ian Shelback for the Little Fox Animal Report in Forest, Canada.

84
00:06:01.495 --> 00:06:08.480
Thank you for joining us and see you next time when we interview another interesting forest animal."
